    contenu: ["Vocabulaire de base : a smartphone, an app (une application), social media (les réseaux sociaux), to post (publier), a follower (un abonné), to scroll (faire défiler), to go viral (devenir viral), a hashtag, an influencer, to livestream (diffuser en direct), an algorithm.", "Avantages souvent cités des réseaux sociaux : staying in touch with friends and family (rester en contact), sharing information quickly, finding communities of people with similar interests, raising awareness about important causes, learning new skills through online tutorials.", "Inconvénients et risques : cyberbullying (le harcèlement en ligne), screen addiction (l'addiction aux écrans), fake news (les fausses informations), privacy issues (les problèmes de vie privée), comparing oneself to others (se comparer aux autres), a negative impact on mental health and sleep.", "Vocabulaire de la cybersécurité : a password (un mot de passe), to hack (pirater), personal data (les données personnelles), to protect your privacy, a scam (une arnaque), to block/report someone (bloquer/signaler quelqu'un).", "Pour structurer un débat en anglais : « On the one hand,... on the other hand,... » (D'un côté... de l'autre...) ; « Some people argue that... whereas others believe that... » ; « In my opinion,... » ; « It seems to me that... » ; « All things considered,... » (Tout bien considéré...).", "Exemple de paragraphe argumentatif : « On the one hand, social media allows teenagers to stay connected and express their creativity. On the other hand, spending too much time online can lead to anxiety and poor sleep. That is why it is important to find a healthy balance and limit screen time. »"],
